      // ============ MAGIC ITEMS (Dungeon Master's Guide 2024 item list) ============
  // Names/types pulled from the published DMG 2024 magic item compendium;
  // descriptions are written fresh for this project (same convention as the
  // rest of this file). Two categories, tagged differently:
  //  - THEMED items (element/domain/construct/aberration/fey-nature-or-trick
  //    keyword match) go to whichever specific type(s) fit, reusing the kind-
  //    overlap trick where valid ("Weapon" covers Celestial+Elemental,
  //    "Treasure" covers Celestial+Fey) since lootTags.kind is one shared
  //    field per row and each type's kind vocabulary is otherwise disjoint.
  //  - GENERIC items (no theme in any direction -- a Bag of Holding, an
  //    Eversmoking Bottle) are deliberately reachable from basically every
  //    balanced type, per the DM: "magic items with no theming can be in
  //    basically any container." Since one row can't carry two DIFFERENT
  //    kind values, a generic item gets a few separate make() calls (same
  //    name, different id) so each type reads its own valid kind.
  // Very Rare/Legendary items are no longer flatly excluded from anywhere --
  // per the DM, that's now a DM-facing checkbox (lootTags.requiresFeature:
  // 'Very Rare+', see monsterTypeFeatures in defaultLootTaxonomy.js) for
  // Celestial, Elemental, and Fey specifically (Dragon/Humanoid/Fiend aren't
  // built out yet; Aberration/Construct were deliberately left off this list,
  // so those two still never see Very Rare+ items, checkbox or not).
  // Artifacts are cataloged but deliberately left untagged -- hand-place
  // these, don't roll them.
